# Command fnm — REMOVED, use mise

## What does this command do:

Nothing here anymore. **fnm is not installed and must not be reinstalled.**

`~/ai/directives/when-building-or-scaffolding-code-in-a-git-repo.md` names **mise** the single
tool version manager on every host and forbids `pyenv`, `rbenv`, `nvm`, `fnm`, `tfenv`,
`tofuenv`, and `goenv` by name.

Removed 2026-08-02: the binary (`~/.local/bin/fnm`), its Node versions
(`~/.local/share/fnm`, v18.18.2 / v20.20.2 / v24.15.0), and the shell fragment
`~/.bash.d/23_bashrc_fedora_fnm`. That fragment loaded *after* `03_mise` and its
`fnm env --use-on-cd` prepend beat the mise shims, so `mise doctor` reported "mise tool paths
are not first in PATH" and every mise-managed Node version was being silently overridden.
See `~/.bash.d/RUNBOOK.md` and the 2026-08-02 entry in `~/ai/fedora/CHANGELOG.md`.

## Command path

None. `command -v fnm` returns nothing, by design.

## Command documentation

mise: https://mise.jdx.dev/ — see also `cheat mise`.

## Command options

# --- fnm -> mise translation ---

# Install a Node version
#   was: fnm install 22 / fnm install --lts / fnm install latest
mise install node@22
mise install node@lts
mise install node@latest

# Use a version in the current directory (writes mise.toml)
#   was: fnm use 22
mise use node@22

# Set the global default (writes ~/.config/mise/config.toml)
#   was: fnm default 22
mise use -g node@22

# List installed versions
#   was: fnm list / fnm ls
mise ls node

# List available remote versions
#   was: fnm list-remote / fnm ls-remote
mise ls-remote node

# Show the active version
#   was: fnm current
mise current node

# Uninstall a version
#   was: fnm uninstall 20
mise uninstall node@20

# Run a command under a specific version without switching
#   was: fnm exec --using 20 node --version
mise x node@20 -- node --version

# --- Auto-switching on cd ---

# fnm needed `--use-on-cd` in shell init. mise does this natively via
# `mise activate` in ~/.bash.d/03_mise — no per-tool hook, and nothing to add.
# Drop a mise.toml in the repo and cd into it:
#
#   [tools]
#   node = "22"

# --- Project version pinning ---

# Do NOT create .node-version or .nvmrc — the directive forbids per-tool version
# files. Pin in mise.toml instead:
mise use node@22        # writes [tools] node = "22" into ./mise.toml

# Verify the config and that declared tools are installed (required pre-commit)
mise doctor
